From: Michael Ludwig <michaelludwig@google.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 14:51:59 -0400
Subject: [M152] [ganesh] Drop unique refs in GrThreadSafeCache when flush
 tasks fail

Original change's description:
> [ganesh] Drop unique refs in GrThreadSafeCache when flush tasks fail
>
> If any render task fails to execute (or instantiation/preFlush fails),
> GrThreadSafeCache entries published ahead of rendering during the flush
> (such as lazy-view blur masks) may point to textures that were never
> initialized. Drop all uniquely-held entries in the thread-safe cache on
> failing flushes so subsequent draws do not consume uninitialized
> textures.
>
> Bug: 561987051
> Fixed: 561987051
> Change-Id: Idff93c3c7ab6480c56f727831d04f7202204c0fd
> Reviewed-on: https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/1368937
> Reviewed-by: Robert Phillips <robertphillips@google.com>
> Commit-Queue: Michael Ludwig <michaelludwig@google.com>

